<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<div type="elementDocumentation" xml:id="elem-functionDates" xmlns:ead="https://archivists.org/ns/ead/v4" xmlns:eac="http://archivists.org/ns/eac/v2" xmlns:eaf="https://archivists.org/ns/eaf/v1" xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3c.org/1999/xlink">
	<head>
		<gi>functionDates</gi>
	</head>
	<div type="fullName">
		<p>Function Dates</p>
	</div>
	<div type="summary">
		<p>An optional element that captures the date or date range, or a combination of date and date range, needed to understand of the function being described.</p>
	</div>
	<div type="mayContain">
		<p>
			<list type="gloss">
				<label>date or dateRange or dateSet</label>
				<item>1..1</item>
			</list>
		</p>
	</div>
	<div type="mayOccurWithin">
		<p>description</p>
	</div>
	<div type="attributes">
		<p>
			<list type="gloss">
				<label>audience</label>
				<item>Optional</item>
				<label>conventionDeclarationReference</label>
				<item>Optional</item>
				<label>id</label>
				<item>Optional</item>
				<label>languageOfElement</label>
				<item>Optional</item>
				<label>maintenanceEventReference</label>
				<item>Optional</item>
				<label>scriptOfElement</label>
				<item>Optional</item>
				<label>sourceReference</label>
				<item>Optional</item>
				<label>target</label>
				<item>Optional</item>
			</list>
		</p>
	</div>
	<div type="description">
		<p><gi>functionDates</gi> is used to assign a specific <gi>date</gi>, for example the creation or revision, of the function being described.</p>
		<p>When a <gi>dateRange</gi> is used this gives information about the whole period the function has been in use. If an open <gi>endDate</gi> is given the described function is seen as being on-going and in current use.</p>
		<p>A combination of <gi>date</gi> and <gi>dateRange</gi> by using the <gi>dateSet</gi> to faciliate more dates needed for dates relating to the described function.</p>
	</div>
	<div type="availability">
		<p>Optional, Not Repeatable</p>
	</div>
	<div type="examples">
		<p>See <gi>eaf</gi> encoding</p>
	</div>
</div>
